          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general General
          %p (…)
          %h3#universal_thom_spectra Universal Thom spectra
          %p
            The universal real Thom spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MO"} MO
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+spectrum"} connective spectrum
            whose associated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+loop+space"} infinite loop space
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi M
                  %mi O
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi Cob
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\infty M O \simeq \vert Cob_\infty \vert .
          %p
            In particular,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mi M
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n M O
            is naturally identified with the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+classes"} cobordism classes
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+theorem"}> Thom's theorem
            ).
          %p
            More abstractly,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MO"} MO
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-homomorphism
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"} Spectra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi O
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M O \simeq \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}(B O \stackrel{J}{\to} B GL_1(\mathbb{S}) \to Spectra)
          %p
            hence the “total space” of the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibration"} spherical fibration
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BO"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O
            for (stable)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+bundles"} real vector bundles
          %p
            Given this, for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            there is a corresponding Thom spectrum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M G \simeq \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}(B G\to B O \stackrel{J}{\to} B GL_1(\mathbb{S}) \to Spectra)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is considered particularly for the stages
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSpin"} MSpin
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MString"} MString
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MFivebrane"} MFivebrane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MNinebrane"} MNinebrane
            and so on.
          %p
            All these Thom spectra happen to naturally have the structure of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            and
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi O
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O\to E
            into another
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            are equivalently universal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientations in E-cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            these are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genera"} genera
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the underlying ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(E)
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#ForVectorBundles For vector bundles
          %p
            First recall the following two basic facts about the construction of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spaces"} Thom spaces
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Thom+space#SuspensionOfThomSpaces"} this prop.
          #SuspensionOfThomSpaces.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+bundle"} real vector bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Th(\mathbb{R}^n \oplus V) \simeq S^n \wedge Th(V) = \Sigma^n Th(V)
            %p
              between, on the one hand, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and, on the other, the
              = succeed "-fold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspension"} reduced suspension
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          #ThomSpaceOfExternalProductOfVectorBundles.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \to X_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_2 \to X_2
              two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+bundles"} real vector bundles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊠
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \boxtimes V_2 \to X_1 \times X_2
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
              of their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+bundle"} pullbacks
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \times X_2
              (their
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/external+tensor+product"} external tensor product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
              of the individual Thom spaces:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊠
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Th(V_1 \boxtimes V_2)
                    \\simeq
                    Th(V_1) \wedge Th(V_2)
                    \\,.
          %p
            Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuspensionOfThomSpaces"}
            will give rise to universal Thom spectra in the following, while Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ThomSpaceOfExternalProductOfVectorBundles"}
            will give them the struture of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
          #ThomSpectrumOfAVectorBundle.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+bundle"} real vector bundle
              %strong Thom spectrum
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty Th(V)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuspensionOfThomSpaces"}
              this may be written as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Sigma^\infty Th(V))_n
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Th(\mathbb{R}^n \oplus V)
            %p
              with structure maps (as a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectrum"} sequential spectrum
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma_n
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\Sigma Th(\mathbb{R}^n \oplus V)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
