            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            structure is that it arises as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
            of a homomorphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+spaces"} E-∞ spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mi Line
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to A Line
            (
            %a{:href => "#ABG10"}> ABG 10, prop.6.21
            ).
          %h3#relation_to_the_cobordism_ring Relation to the cobordism ring
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_10 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism group
              of un
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oriented"} oriented
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "al" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally isomorphic
              to the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
              of the Thom spectrum
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                      %mi un
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo →
                        %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^{un}_\bullet \simeq \pi_\bullet M O
                    \\coloneqq
                    {\lim_{\to}}_{k \to \infty} \pi_{n+k} M O(k)
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is a seminal result due to (
            %a{:href => "#Thom54"}> Thom 54
            ), whose proof proceeds by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+construction"} Pontryagin-Thom construction
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Francis3"} Francis, lecture 3
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              We first construct a map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Θ
                      %mo :
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi n
                        %mi un
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mi M
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta : \Omega_n^{un} \to \pi_n M O
            %p
              Given a class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi n
                      %mi un
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X] \in \Omega_n^{un}
              we can choose a representative
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+embedding"} closed embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n+k}
              of sufficiently large
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighbourhood+theorem"} tubular neighbourhood theorem
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu
              factors as the embedding of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+section"} zero section
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} normal bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_\nu
              followed by an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+embedding"} open embedding
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_\nu
              into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n+k}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↪
                              %mi ν
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi ν
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;&amp;\stackrel{\nu}{\hookrightarrow}&amp;&amp; \mathbb{R}^{n+k}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{i}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; N_\nu
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now use the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+construction"} Pontrjagin-Thom construction
              to produce an element of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
              first in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th(N_\nu)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_\nu
              and then eventually in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n+k} \to (\mathbb{R}^{n+k})^+ \simeq S^{n+k}
            %p
              be the map into the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo →
                    %mi Disk
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Sphere
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    t : S^{n+k} \simeq (\mathbb{R}^{n+k})^+ \to Disk(N_\nu)/Sphere(N_\nu) \simeq Th(N_\nu)
            %p
              by sending points in the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Disk
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disk(N_\nu)
              under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              to their preimage, and all other points to the collapsed point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sphere
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sphere(N_\nu)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Th
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi ν
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n+k}(Th(N_\nu))
            %p
              To turn this into an element in the homotopy group of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M O
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_\nu
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              by a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              of the universal rank
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              vector bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi γ
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma_k \to B O(k)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi ν
                            %mo ≃
                            %msup
                              %mi μ
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi γ
                              %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi μ
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mi O
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    N_\nu \simeq \mu^* \gamma_k &amp;\to&amp; \gamma_k
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\mu}{\to}&amp; B O(k)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p By forming Thom spaces the top map induces a map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo :
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Th(N_\nu) \to Th(\gamma^k) =: M O(k)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Its composite with the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              constructed above gives an element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n+k} M O(k)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi t
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^{n+k} \stackrel{t}{\to} Th(N_\nu) \to Th(\gamma^k) \simeq M O(k)
            %p
              and by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n+k} M O(k) \to {\lim_\to}_k \pi_{n+k} M O(k) =: \pi_n M O
              this is finally an element
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi t
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi ν
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Theta
                    \:
                    [X]
                    \\mapsto
                    (S^{n+k} \stackrel{t}{\to} Th(N_\nu) \to Th(\gamma^k) \simeq M O(k))
                    \\in
                    \\pi_n M O
                    \\,.
            %p
              We show now that this element does not depend on the choice of embedding
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ν
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu : X \to \mathbb{R}^{n+k}
            %p (…)
            %p
              Finally, to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              we proceed by constructing an inverse.
            %p
              For that, observe that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n+k}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact topological space
              and in fact a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{n+k}
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi s
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi s
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Th(\gamma^k)  \simeq {\lim_\to}_s Th(\gamma^k_s)
                    \\,,
            %p factors through one of the terms as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi s
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f : S^{n+k} \to Th(\gamma^k_s) \hookrightarrow Th(\gamma^k)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom%27s+transversality+theorem"} Thom's transversality theorem
              we may find an embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Gr
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi γ
                      %mi s
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : Gr_k(\mathbb{R}^s) \to Th(\gamma^k_s)
              by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transverse+map"} transverse map
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Gr
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mi k
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Th
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi γ
                              %mi s
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; Gr_k(\mathbb{R}^s)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}}
                    \\\
                    S^{n+k} &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Th(\gamma^k_s)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              We check that this construction provides an inverse to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta
            %p (…)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi M
                    %mi O
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi Cob
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\infty M O \simeq \vert Cob_\infty \vert
              is the content of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galatius-Madsen-Tillmann-Weiss+theorem"} Galatius-Madsen-Tillmann-Weiss theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
              theorem.
          %h3#AsDualObject As a dual in the stable homotopy category
          %p
            Write
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spec"} Spec
            for the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spec)
            for its standard
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            this becomes a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spec)
            by forming its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+spectrum"} suspension spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty_+ X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            this is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dualizable object
            with respect to the smash-product monoidal structure.
          %p
            It turns out that a sufficient condition is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            or more generally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            Euclidean
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood+retract"} neighbourhood retract
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Th
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th(N X)
            – the Thom spectrum of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+bundle"} stable normal bundle
            is the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dual object
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Atiyah61"} Atiyah 61
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#DoldPuppe78"} Dold-Puppe 78
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spanier-Whitehead+dual"} Spanier-Whitehead dual
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo +
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty_+ X
          %p
            Using this one shows that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
            of the identity on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty_+ X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Spec)
            – the categorical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo +
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty_+ X
            – is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            For a brief exposition see (
            %a{:href => "#PontoShulman"}> PontoShulman, example 3.7
            ). For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spanier-Whitehead+duality"} Spanier-Whitehead duality
          %h3#AsTheUniversalSphericalFibration
            As the universal spherical fibration, from the
            = succeed "-homomorphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-homomorphism
            is a canonical map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi gl
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O \to B gl_1(\mathbb{S})
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+orthogonal+group"} stable orthogonal group
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group+of+units"} infinity-group of units
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-vector+bundle"} (∞,1)-vector bundle
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectrum"} modules
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B O
            and this is the Thom spectrum.
          %p
            So in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
            description
            %a{:href => "#ForInfinityModuleBundles"} above
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi O
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mi O
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi J
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo =
                  %mi Spectra
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M O \simeq  \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}(B O \stackrel{J}{\to} B GL_1(\mathbb{S}) \to \mathbb{S}Mod = Spectra)
                  \\,.
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
            for more on this.
          %h3#AsTheInfiniteCobordismCategory As the infinite cobordism category
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (infinity,n)-category of cobordisms
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \to \infty
            is the Thom spectrum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi MO
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\vert Bord_\infty \vert \simeq \Omega^\infty MO
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is implied by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galatius-Madsen-Tillmann-Weiss+theorem"} Galatius-Madsen-Tillmann-Weiss theorem
            and by
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"} Jacob Lurie
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Francis3"} Francis-Gwilliam, remark 0.9
          %h2#cohomology Cohomology
          %p
            Under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
            the Thom spectrum represents the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theory called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory"} cobordism theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"}> Thom space
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin-Thom+collapse+map"} Pontryagin-Thom collapse map
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
          %p
            %br/
          %div
            %p
              %strong>
                flavors of
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theories"} bordism homology theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theories"} cobordism cohomology theories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} representing
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectra"} Thom spectra
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+rings"} cobordism rings
              \:
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+homology+theory"} bordism theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M%28B%2Cf%29"} M(B,f)
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-bordism"}> B-bordism
              ):
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MFr"} MFr
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MO"}> MO
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSO"} MSO
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSpin"} MSpin
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MString"} MString
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MFivebrane"} MFivebrane
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MNinebrane"} MNinebrane
                  …
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"}> MU
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSU"} MSU
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ravenel%27s+spectrum"} MΩΩSU(n)
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MP-theory"}> MP
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MR-theory"} MR
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSpin%5Ec"}>
                    MSpin
                    %sup
                      %i c
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSpin%5Eh"}
                    MSpin
                    %sup
                      %i h
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSp"} MSp
            %p relative bordism theories:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MOFr"}> MOFr
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MUFr"} MUFr
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSUFr"} MSUFr
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+bordism+homology+theory"}> equivariant bordism theory
              \:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+MFr"} equivariant MFr
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+MO"} equivariant MO
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+MU"} equivariant MU
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+bordism+homology+theory"}> global equivariant bordism theory
              \:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+mO"}> global equivariant mO
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+mU"} global equivariant mU
            %p algebraic:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+cobordism"} algebraic cobordism
          %p
            %br/
          %div
            %p The following terms all refer to essentially the same concept:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+generalized+cohomology"} fiber integration in generalized cohomology
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/push-forward+in+generalized+cohomology"} push-forward in generalized cohomology
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Umkehr+map"}> Umkehr map
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Umkehr+map"} twisted Umkehr map
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gysin+map"} Gysin map
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+collapse+map"} Pontrjagin-Thom collapse map
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general_2 General
          %p The relation between the homotopy groups of the Thom spectrum and the cobordism ring is due to
          %ul
            %li#Thom54
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ren%C3%A9+Thom"}> René Thom
              ,
              %em Quelques propriétés globales des variétés différentiables
              Comment. Math. Helv. 28, (1954). 17-86
          %p Further original articles include
          %ul
            %li#Atiyah61
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Thom complexes
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/atiyahthom.pdf"} pdf
          %p Textbook accounts include
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
                , part III, section 2 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
            %li#Kochmann96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochman"}> Stanley Kochman
                , section 1.5 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
          %p Lecture notes include
          %ul
            %li#Francis3
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"}> John Francis
                ,
                %em Topology of manifolds
                course notes (2010) (
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/"}> web
                )
              %p
                Lecture 3
                %em Thom’s theorem
                (notes by A. Smith) (
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/3thom.pdf"}> pdf
                )
              %p
                A remark of the relation of the Thom spectrum to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (∞,n)-category of cobordisms
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = \infty
                is in:
              %p
                Lecture 2
                %em Cobordisms
                (notes by
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"} Owen Gwilliam
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/2cobordism.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Ebert12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johannes+Ebert"}> Johannes Ebert
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A lecture course on Cobordism Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://wwwmath.uni-muenster.de/u/jeber_02/skripten/bordism-skript.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Freed13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
                , lecture 10 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bordism: old and new
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/bordism.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            As
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
          %ul
            %li#HoveyShipleySmith00
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Hovey"}> Mark Hovey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith"} Jeff Smith
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Symmetric spectra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9801077"} arXiv:math/9801077
            %li#Schlichtkrull09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christian+Schlichtkrull"}> Christian Schlichtkrull
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Thom Spectra that Are Symmetric Spectra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0811.0592"} arXiv:0811.0592
            %li#Schwede12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                , Example I.2.6 in
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Symmetric spectra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~schwede/SymSpec.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            As
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            and as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+spectra"} equivariant spectra
          %ul
            %li#Schwede15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              , chapter V.4 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Global+homotopy+theory"} Global homotopy theory
          %p
            Textbook discussion with an eye towards the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Rudyak98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuli+Rudyak"}> Yuli Rudyak
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Thom spectra, orientability and cobordism
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9"} doi:10.1007/978-3-540-77751-9
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/rudyakthom.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Quinn"}> Frank Quinn
              ,
              %em Assembly maps in bordism-type theories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/quinnass.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A generalized notion of Thom spectra in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-module+bundles"} (∞,1)-module bundles
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#ABGHR
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"} Andrew Blumberg
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Charles Rezk
              %em Units of ring spectra and Thom spectra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0810.4535"}> arXiv:0810.4535
              )
          %p a streamlined update of which is
          %ul
            %li#ABGHR14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"} Andrew Blumberg
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Charles Rezk
              %em
                An
                = succeed "-categorical" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "-line" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                = succeed "-homology" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1403.4325"}> arXiv:1403.4325
              )
          %p
            Discussion of Thom spectra from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-module+bundles"} (∞,1)-module bundles
            is in
          %ul
            %li#ABG10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Blumberg"} Andrew Blumberg
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twists of K-theory and TMF
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"} Jonathan Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Superstrings, Geometry, Topology, and
                  = succeed "-algebras" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mo *
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/bookstore-getitem/item=PSPUM-81"} vol 81
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3004"} arXiv:1002.3004
          %p which is reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#Wilson13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dylan+Wilson"}> Dylan Wilson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Thom spectra from the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  point of view
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.northwestern.edu/~bwill/thom/DWthom4.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"} motivic quantization
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+generalized+cohomology"} pushforward
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology"} generalized cohomology
            in section 3.1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joost+Nuiten"}> Joost Nuiten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/master+thesis+Nuiten"} Cohomological quantization of local prequantum boundary field theory
          %h3#as_dual_objects_in_the_stable_homotopy_category As dual objects in the stable homotopy category
          %p
            The relation of Thom spectra to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+objects"} dualizable objects
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
